<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">French Committee of National Liberation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1943–1944</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The French Committee of National Liberation was formed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> in June 1943, uniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a>'s Free French with the forces of General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-giraud">Henri Giraud</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. It acted as the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> outside German control, directing French forces and the Resistance, and de Gaulle soon became its sole leader. In June 1944 it became the Provisional Government of the French Republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/french-committee-of-national-liberation.jpg" alt="French Committee of National Liberation" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:De_Gaulle-Giraud_shot0092.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
